The AI provider and its model
gettingstarted-24-the-ai-helper
One provider and one model serve the account. The check box marks the provider in use; none marked means the AI is off. Anthropic, OpenAI, Google and DeepSeek come with their connection details and a default model filled in: you supply the key. Custom is the fifth choice, where you fill in everything yourself, the model included.
S opens the setup dialog for the provider under the cursor. It looks the same every time: the Key, the Model and Other name. The key is a password field: what you type or paste is shown as *, and when a key is already set the field shows a row of stars that keeps it. The Model is a list of the provider's own model names, with the one in use chosen. With no key yet, enter the key and press Tab: the key goes to the AI helper and the list is filled from the provider with it. Other name is only for a model the list does not hold, such as on a Custom server that gives no list. Save sets what you chose. Model names are case-sensitive: a model set with the wrong capitals is pointed out and the listed one chosen.
The key is kept by the AI helper (a private file in your Solo directory, mode 0600) and sent only to the provider's address over https, with the certificate checked. A key typed in the dialog passes through your SD session on its way: it goes to the helper through a file in a directory only you can enter, which is removed at once; it is never on a command line or in the audit trail. To keep a key out of SD altogether, type it at the helper's own prompt instead: set.ai key PROVIDER.
Selecting a provider means that the text the account sends leaves this machine for that provider. It can send text only if the ai gate is on (the Account box). Nothing is on as delivered: no provider, no key and the gate off.
Enter selects or deselects the provider. S sets it up (key and model), X clears the key, C fills in Custom, D removes it, A sets the file of certificate authorities for a private CA, L changes a limit. At the prompt: set.ai.
T opens the standing text: a few lines sent first with every AI request, telling the AI what SD is and where its help is. SD ships a default; edit it and choose Save to send your own, or Shipped default to go back. It is not shown when you ask the AI and does not change your question. A text that names SD's own code is refused.
